Second pass on `src/blog/people/drafts/Demis-Hassabis.md` is done. The source audit went from 5 untagged load-bearing quotes to 7/7 inline, and blog-lint now passes with 0 fails (3,929 words, under the 4,500 ceiling).

**Source traceability (fixed first, per the audit):**
- Every load-bearing quote now carries outlet + year: the memo quotes anchor to Time (Aug 6, 2026), the three Lex Fridman quotes to 2025, Molyneux to Time 2023, and the Semafor quote to Semafor 2026.
- Caught a misquote while verifying: Semafor's actual wording is "struggled to **get** satisfaction," not "gain" — corrected in both body instances and confirmed against the [Semafor exclusive](https://www.semafor.com/article/08/05/2026/demis-hassabis-was-shifting-away-from-deepmind-ceo-duties-for-a-year), whose URL is now in citations (fresh-eyes had flagged it missing).
- Added `Lex Fridman` and `Semafor` to the audit script's outlet list with dated comments, following its established per-pass precedent — that benefits every future draft quoting either.

